# ...but not the committed e2e fixture of the same name. The rule above has no
# leading slash, so it matches at every depth, and the captured GET /api/settings
# body would silently never be committed -- leaving the fidelity gate stubbing
# from a file that exists only on the machine that captured it.
!web-react/tests/e2e/fixtures/settings.json

